it's official roughly two months after  valorent pro  j sinatra wan was accused of sexual  assault and sexual misconduct by an  ex-girlfriend  developer riot games has handed the  sentinels player a six-month competitive  ban  riot games also stated it had quote  serious concerns regarding his conduct  during its investigation  and that he would need to complete quote  professional conduct training  prior to his return  on monday may 17th riot games published  a statement regarding the status of  sentinel's valorant player sinatra  quote jay sinatra juan has violated rule  8.1 of the ballarant global competition  policy  for failing to fully cooperate with the  tournament operator's investigation  and will be suspended for six months he  will also be required to complete  professional conduct training  end quote now rule 8.1 of valoran's  global competition policy  reads as follows quote by agreeing to  this global policy  each team member agrees to cooperate  with the tournament operator in any  internal or external investigation  that the tournament operator conducts  relating to a suspected violation of  this global policy  the applicable event-specific rules or  applicable law  end quote what's important to note here  is that this statement and ruling  does not find sinatra innocent or guilty  of the sexual assault and sexual  misconduct allegations that he was  accused of back in march  furthermore riot stated that when it  comes to these allegations they'd be  deferring to law enforcement  or waiting for quote additional material  information  to come to light the suspension stems  specifically from the fact that  according to  riot sinatra did not fully cooperate  with them during its investigation  into these allegations despite publicly  stating that he would do so  quote while the investigation did not  come to a definitive conclusion on the  underlying allegations  the competitive operations team had  serious concerns with sinatra's conduct  during the course of the investigation  it was determined that  on at least two occasions sinatra  misrepresented certain facts  made false statements and did not  cooperate with the investigation  in a way expected of a professional  ballerin esports player  of note sinatra's public commitment on  social media to provide the full  audio and video clip referenced in the  original post  was never fulfilled cooperation in these  investigations is of the utmost  importance  especially when the nature of the  allegations is as serious as sexual  assault  this behavior will not be tolerated by  valor and esports  end quote let's talk about the audio and  video clip riot is referring to  and therefore the sexual assault and  sexual misconduct allegations he was  accused of  back in march back on march 9th  sinatra's ex-girlfriend cleo hernandez  published a thorough nine page document  accusing sinatra of sexual assault  and sexual misconduct as part of that  document hernandez included an audio  clip and subsequent transcript of a  situation  where sinatra allegedly forced her to  continue having sex with him  despite stating repeatedly that she  didn't want to we covered this situation  back on this show when the document was  published  she alleges that over the course of that  time he made unwanted sexual advances  after she told him not to she felt like  saying no to sex was  never an option he would continue to  have sex with her after she told him to  stop and was in pain  he acted manipulatively and guilted her  into having sex  after she said no he was emotionally  abusive he would check her location  using his iphone  and if it didn't match where she said  she was he would accuse her of cheating  and that she lived in constant fear of  him a short time later sinatra published  his own statement denying ever  assaulting cleo  and saying that he would cooperate fully  with the investigation  quote i am fully cooperating with the  investigations and providing the full  audio and video clips clio referenced in  her post  end quote sentinels responded by  suspending him  pending the conclusion of riot's  investigation here's sentinel's  statement  quote we are aware of the current  situation regarding j sinatra 1  and have launched an investigation  internally while the investigation is  pending  he is suspended from the team we will  provide a  further update once the investigation  has concluded end quote  so coming back to riot's statement  according to them he did not provide the  full audio and video clips  like he said he would in his original  statement furthermore  whatever facts sinatra allegedly  misrepresented  and false statements he made to riot  during its investigation  none of that has been made public at the  moment it should also be noted that it's  unclear whether or not  riot's investigation is closed as  they've stated that these allegations  are being investigated by  law enforcement and riot will be  deferring to them  quote during the course of the fact  gathering the competitive operations  team  was informed that the matter had been  referred to law enforcement  so at this juncture we will defer to the  authorities to make further  investigation into and factual findings  related to the allegations  end quote now we first learned about law  enforcement's involvement when cleo  published a subsequent document on  tuesday april 20th  expanding on her original allegations  and confirming the existence of a police  report  and ongoing legal investigation i  reached out to washington dc police at  the time hoping to acquire a copy of  that police report  based on the information available they  found one police report filed by someone  named cleo hernandez on march 12th  of this year i was unable to obtain any  further information due to the fact that  the investigation is still ongoing  and because the alleged incident took  place in another jurisdiction  not dc now here's what riot does say  regarding its potentially still  ongoing investigation quote to the  extent that additional material  information comes to light  from law enforcement or otherwise the  competitive operations team reserves the  right to reopen the investigation  and take further appropriate action end  quote now we're not 100  sure that riot's investigation is  definitively closed  but that last statement i just read you  implies  to me anyway that riot's investigation  seems to be closed  unless the law enforcement investigation  provides  new information that would cause riot to  re-open their initial investigation  now according to riot sinatra's  suspension began on march 10th  and therefore will run until september  10 2021  making him technically eligible to  compete for the last chance qualifiers  and champions shortly after riot  published its statement sinatra released  his own twitlonger  here's the opening paragraph of that  quote i've spent the last two months  reflecting on how i can be better as a  person i've been a pro player for  basically all of my adult life  and still have a lot to improve on i've  been reflecting a ton during the down  time  and know how much i hurt cleo  emotionally and i'm truly sorry about it  i will learn from my mistakes  and keep on trying to improve myself as  a person end quote  from there he addressed riot's statement  and said that he never had the audio or  video clips in question  that he deleted them after he and cleo  broke up which he  says was done at her request i want to  preface this by saying i do not have the  video or audio that she used in her  statement  after our relationship ended she asked  me to delete the video and i honored  that  i never even imagined a situation like  this so when it all happened  i didn't know whether to just spill out  my side or not i had no clue what to do  so i seeked legal help immediately as we  were drafting up an  update with the legal pr team we had  added that i would provide the video  because we genuinely thought that the  video would have to be shared in full  since it's a key part in the  investigation end quote  from there he apologized again and said  that he'll use the next four months to  develop quote  a better set of interpersonal skills and  to earn back the trust of this community  end quote roughly 24 hours after sinatra  published his twitlonger responding to  riot games's statement  cleo hernandez who you'll remember is  sinatra's ex-girlfriend that accused him  responded to his twit longer with her  own twitter  in it she says that she never asked him  to delete the audio or video clips  and that she says she would have  welcomed him sharing that with riot's  investigation  quote i'll start by saying that i never  once told him to delete the video  i did not care whatsoever if he kept it  or not i thought he still had it and i  told the riot investigators that i  welcomed him showing the video  because in it you can see his fingers  dig into me when i try and move away  from him  he took the video and he sent it to me  it was just in our text thread because i  never delete text  from there cleo says that she would have  provided the full audio and video clips  if she was requested to but according to  her she never was  on top of that she says that she will  never accept his apology  and that the legal investigation has  been a long process  one that's been quite traumatic for her  to go through quote  so yes he refused to comply with the  investigation was caught in multiple  lies and didn't give a video that  wouldn't have proved his innocence  he gave an apology that i will never at  any point in my life be accepting of  because it is entirely too late the  legal aspect will develop slowly and  depends entirely on my emotional  strength when it comes to dealing with  law enforcement and detectives  which has so far been one of the most  traumatizing things i've ever done  in my life end quote from there cleo  ends the twitlonger basically saying  that at this point she wants to move on  and not have to keep putting out  statements like this what's still  unknown at this point is how  sentinels the org he still technically  signed to  will respond they haven't posted any  statement to social media  and i reached out to them for comment  but didn't hear back in time for  publication  it also raises questions about tenza's  tenure with the org he's been filling in  for sinatra since he was originally  suspended  in that time tens has helped sentinels  win both masters 1  and challenger finals he will also be  competing with the org  at the upcoming masters ii lan in  iceland beginning on may 25th  i also emailed riot in the hopes that  they would clarify the statement that  they published  but i didn't hear back in time for  publication  [Music]  you
 

